From: EasyMesh Lab <easymesh-lab@localhost>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi_hal: request ACKs for unicast action frames

The generic management-frame API sent every action frame with noack=1.
For a unicast BTM Request this sets NL80211_ATTR_DONT_WAIT_FOR_ACK and
disables normal acknowledgement/retry handling.  A transient loss then
looks like a successful request throughout the upper layers.

Request ACK handling for unicast action frames and retain no-ACK behavior
only for group-addressed frames, which cannot be acknowledged.
---
 wifi_hal.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/wifi_hal.c b/wifi_hal.c
--- a/wifi_hal.c
+++ b/wifi_hal.c
@@ -4671,6 +4671,7 @@ int wifi_hal_send_mgmt_frame(int apIndex,mac_address_t sta, const unsigned char
     u8 *buf;
     struct ieee80211_hdr *hdr;
     int res = 0;
+    int noack;
 #ifdef HOSTAPD_2_11 // 2.11
     int link_id = 0;
 #endif
@@ -4696,14 +4697,23 @@ int wifi_hal_send_mgmt_frame(int apIndex,mac_address_t sta, const unsigned char
         os_memcpy(hdr->addr3, interface->u.sta.backhaul.bssid, ETH_ALEN);
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Unicast action frames, including BSS Transition Management requests,
+     * need normal 802.11 acknowledgement and retry handling.  Setting
+     * DONT_WAIT_FOR_ACK for those frames turns an intermittent RF loss into a
+     * silent steering miss.  Retain no-ACK behavior only for group-addressed
+     * management frames, which cannot be acknowledged.
+     */
+    noack = (sta[0] & 0x01) ? 1 : 0;
+
     
 #ifdef HOSTAPD_2_11 // 2.11
     link_id = wifi_hal_get_mld_link_id(interface);
-    res = wifi_drv_send_mlme(interface, buf, 24 + data_len, 1, freq, NULL, 0, 0, wait, link_id);
+    res = wifi_drv_send_mlme(interface, buf, 24 + data_len, noack, freq, NULL, 0, 0, wait, link_id);
 #elif HOSTAPD_2_10 // 2.10
-    res = wifi_drv_send_mlme(interface, buf, 24 + data_len, 1, freq, NULL, 0, 0, wait);
+    res = wifi_drv_send_mlme(interface, buf, 24 + data_len, noack, freq, NULL, 0, 0, wait);
 #else
-    res = wifi_drv_send_mlme(interface, buf, 24 + data_len, 1, freq, NULL, 0);
+    res = wifi_drv_send_mlme(interface, buf, 24 + data_len, noack, freq, NULL, 0);
 #endif
 
     os_free(buf);
-- 
